    "narrative": "This Suspicious Activity Report (SAR) documents unauthorized credit card fraud identified on customer account C04570. On 2016-11-11 23:46:24, flagged transaction 3450629 for $100.09 was detected via online channel with an elevated risk score of 0.57. Graph analytics and multi-hop link expansion revealed that the transaction was associated with device profile 'Windows | Windows 10 | chrome 65.0 | 1920x1080', which was identified across 298 additional cardholder accounts (C00163-K1, C00180-K1, C00219-K1). The cardholder, when contacted for transaction validation, confirmed they did not authorize the transactions and remained in possession of their physical card. The activity exhibits characteristics consistent with undocumented, where compromised credentials or card data were systematically exploited. Total cumulative fraudulent exposure across identified affected transactions (3450629) totals $100.09. The financial institution has taken immediate mitigating actions by blocking card C04570-K1 for reissue, opening internal case HHG-017 in graph memory, and placing all connected card accounts under continuous surveillance per Bank Policy R2, R6, and regulatory guidelines.",
